.TH mbpy_plot 1 "3 November 2026" "MB-System 5.0" "MB-System 5.0"
.SH NAME
\fBmbpy_plot\fP \- Create an executable shellscript which will generate
a GMT modern-mode map of swath sonar data.

.SH VERSION
Version 5.0

.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmbpy_plot\fP [\fB\-I\fP\fIfile\fP] [\fB\-F\fP\fIformat\fP]
[\fB\-O\fP\fIroot\fP]
[\fB\-\-format\fP \fIfmt\fP]
[\fB\-\-title\fP \fItext\fP]
[\fB\-\-colorbar\-label\fP \fItext\fP]
[\fB\-\-dpi\fP \fIdpi\fP]
[\fB\-X\fP] [\fB\-V\fP]
.br
[\fB\-R\fP\fIwest/east/south/north\fP]
[\fB\-J\fP\fIspec\fP]
[\fB\-P\fP\fIpagesize\fP]
[\fB\-\-portrait\fP | \fB\-\-landscape\fP]
[\fB\-\-scale\-location\fP \fIl|r|t|b\fP]
[\fB\-\-tick\-info\fP \fIspec\fP]
[\fB\-\-length\-scale\fP \fIspec\fP]
[\fB\-\-timestamp\fP [\fIlabel\fP]]
.br
[\fB\-G\fP\fIcolor_mode\fP] [\fB\-\-filtered\fP]
[\fB\-W\fP\fIcolor_style/palette\fP[\fI/ncolors\fP] | \fIcptfile\fP]
[\fB\-D\fP] [\fB\-Y\fP] [\fB\-S\fP]
[\fB\-Z\fP\fImin/max\fP]
.br
[\fB\-A\fP\fImagnitude\fP[\fI/azimuth\fP | \fI/zero_level\fP]]
[\fB\-\-magnitude\fP \fIval\fP]
[\fB\-\-azimuth\fP \fIdeg\fP]
[\fB\-\-zero\-level\fP \fIval\fP]
[\fB\-\-shade\-flip\fP]
[\fB\-\-stretch\-shade\fP]
.br
[\fB\-C\fP[\fIcont_int/color_int/tick_int/label_int/tick_len/label_hgt\fP]]
[\fB\-\-contour\-algorithm\fP \fIn\fP]
[\fB\-\-contour\-nplot\fP \fIpings\fP]
.br
[\fB\-N\fP[\fItime_tick/time_annot/date_annot/tick_len\fP | \fBF\fP | \fBFP\fP]]
[\fB\-\-nav\-names\fP [\fIheight\fP[\fI/P\fP]]]
[\fB\-\-ping\-ticks\fP [\fItick/annot/len\fP]]
.br
[\fB\-\-footprint\fP \fIfactor/mode/depth\fP]
[\fB\-\-swath\-scale\fP \fImode/scale\fP[\fI/min/max\fP]]
[\fB\-\-begin\-time\fP \fIyr/mo/da/hr/mn/sc\fP]
[\fB\-\-end\-time\fP \fIyr/mo/da/hr/mn/sc\fP]
[\fB\-\-speedmin\fP \fIspeed\fP]
[\fB\-\-timegap\fP \fIminutes\fP]
[\fB\-\-lonflip\fP \fI\-1|0|1\fP]
.br
[\fB\-T\fP] [\fB\-\-coast\-resolution\fP \fIres\fP]
[\fB\-\-coast\-dry\-fill\fP \fIcolor\fP]
[\fB\-\-coast\-wet\-fill\fP \fIcolor\fP]
[\fB\-\-coast\-lake\-fill\fP \fIcolor\fP]
[\fB\-\-coast\-river\fP \fIspec\fP]
[\fB\-\-coast\-boundary\fP \fIspec\fP]
[\fB\-\-coast\-pen\fP \fIpen\fP]
.br
[\fB\-\-xy\-overlay\fP \fIfile\fP[\fI:fill=..\fP][\fI:symbol=..\fP][\fI:pen=..\fP]]
[\fB\-\-text\fP \fIlon/lat/size/angle/font/justify/text\fP]
[\fB\-\-gmt\-default\fP \fIparam/value\fP]

.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBmbpy_plot\fP is a Python/PyGMT-era replacement for the Perl macro
\fBmbm_plot\fP. It reads a swath sonar data file, or a datalist of
them, and generates an executable shellscript of \fBGMT\fP \fBmodern
mode\fP commands which, when run, maps the swath data themselves
(rather than a grid made from them) with the \fBMB-System\fP GMT
modules \fBmbswath\fP and \fBmbcontour\fP. The map may include a
bathymetry color fill (\fB\-G1\fP), bathymetry color shaded relief
(\fB\-G2\fP), bathymetry shaded by beam amplitude (\fB\-G3\fP), an
amplitude fill (\fB\-G4\fP) or a sidescan fill (\fB\-G5\fP);
bathymetry contours (\fB\-C\fP); the ship track with time and file name
annotation (\fB\-N\fP); a coastline; xy data drawn as lines or symbols;
text labels; a color scale; and a distance scale. If none of \fB\-G\fP,
\fB\-C\fP and \fB\-N\fP is given, the navigation track is plotted.

The map bounds come from the files' ".inf" files (made by \fBmbinfo\fP
or \fBmbdatalist \-O\fP) when they exist and no time window is given,
and otherwise from running \fBmbinfo\fP; they are padded by 5% and,
if needed, widened so that the map is no more than twice as long as
it is wide. The map is scaled to fit the page size (\fB\-P\fP) in the
orientation that gives the larger map, unless the projection or scale
is given with \fB\-J\fP. Page layout and projection fitting are shared
with \fBmbpy_grdplot\fP.

The generated script is named \fIroot\fP.sh and makes
\fIroot\fP.\fIfmt\fP (\fBpdf\fP by default). A generated color palette
is written to \fIroot\fP.cpt (and, for a stretched amplitude shade,
\fIroot\fP.shade.cpt) by \fBmbpy_plot\fP itself. When the input is a
single swath file rather than a datalist, the script makes and then
removes a one-line datalist \fIroot\fP_datalist.mb\-1 for it. No gmt.conf
file is created or deleted in the current directory.

As in \fBmbpy_grdplot\fP, the colon-separated \fB\-M\fP\fIsub\fP
options of \fBmbm_plot\fP are replaced by descriptive long options.
Palettes are limited to 1-7, as in \fBmbm_plot\fP.

\fBmbpy_plot\fP requires \fBGMT\fP 6 or later with the \fBMB-System\fP
GMT modules, and a Python 3 interpreter. It uses the modules
\fBmbpy_layout.py\fP, \fBmbpy_color.py\fP, \fBmbpy_misc.py\fP,
\fBmbpy_grdplot_script.py\fP and \fBmbpy_plot_script.py\fP, installed
alongside it.

