.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-I\fP, \fB\-\-input\fP \fIfile\fP
Swath data file or datalist. Default: datalist.mb\-1.
.TP
.B \-F\fP, \fB\-\-data\-format\fP \fIformat\fP
\fBMB-System\fP format id of the input file, or \-1 for a datalist.
Default: determined with \fBmbformat\fP.
.TP
.B \-O\fP, \fB\-\-output\fP \fIroot\fP
Output root name. Default: the input's basename without its extension.
.TP
.B \-\-format\fP \fIfmt\fP
Output format passed to \fBgmt begin\fP: pdf, png, ps, jpg, tif, eps,
\&... Default \fBpdf\fP.
.TP
.B \-\-title\fP \fItext\fP
Map title. Default: "Data List File \fIfile\fP" or "Data File
\fIfile\fP".
.TP
.B \-\-colorbar\-label\fP \fItext\fP
Color scale label. Default: "Depth (meters)", "Beam Amplitude Values"
or "Sidescan Pixel Values", by color mode.
.TP
.B \-\-dpi\fP \fIdpi\fP
Resolution of the \fBmbswath\fP image (\fBmbswath \-E\fP) and of a
raster output file.
.TP
.B \-X\fP, \fB\-\-execute
Run the generated script immediately after writing it.
.TP
.B \-V\fP, \fB\-\-verbose
Print progress and a summary of the map.
.TP
.B \-R\fP, \fB\-\-region\fP \fIwest/east/south/north\fP
Map bounds in longitude and latitude. Default: the data bounds,
padded as described above.
.TP
.B \-J\fP, \fB\-\-projection\fP \fIspec\fP
GMT map projection with a scale or width, e.g. \fBm1.0\fP or
\fBM6i\fP; giving only the projection lets \fBmbpy_plot\fP choose the
scale. Default: a Mercator projection scaled to fill the page.
.TP
.B \-P\fP, \fB\-\-pagesize\fP \fIpagesize\fP
Page size code (a, b, c, d, e, f, e1, a0-a10, b0-b10, c0-c7, m1-m6),
as in \fBmbm_plot\fP. Default \fBa\fP.
.TP
.B \-\-portrait\fP, \fB\-\-landscape
Force the page orientation instead of choosing it automatically.
.TP
.B \-\-scale\-location\fP \fIl|r|t|b\fP
Place the color scale at the left, right, top or bottom of the map.
Default \fBb\fP.
.TP
.B \-\-tick\-info\fP \fIspec\fP
Raw \fB\-B\fP basemap tick-interval spec, replacing the computed one.
.TP
.B \-\-length\-scale\fP \fIspec\fP
Draw a distance scale with \fBgmt basemap \-L\fP\fIspec\fP, e.g.
"jBL+c36.8+w5k+o0.3/0.3". The word "center" in \fIspec\fP is replaced
by the longitude/latitude of the map center, e.g. "gcenter+c36.8+w5k".
.TP
.B \-\-timestamp\fP [\fIlabel\fP]
Add a GMT time stamp (\fB\-U\fP), with an optional label.
.TP
.B \-G\fP, \fB\-\-color\-mode\fP \fIcolor_mode\fP
Swath image style (\fBmbswath \-Z\fP):
.br
  \fIcolor_mode\fP = 1: Bathymetry color fill.
.br
  \fIcolor_mode\fP = 2: Bathymetry color shaded relief.
.br
  \fIcolor_mode\fP = 3: Bathymetry color shaded by beam amplitude.
.br
  \fIcolor_mode\fP = 4: Beam amplitude fill.
.br
  \fIcolor_mode\fP = 5: Sidescan fill.
.TP
.B \-\-filtered
Plot filtered amplitude or sidescan values (\fBmbswath
\-Z\fP\fImode\fP\fBF\fP).
.TP
.B \-W\fP, \fB\-\-color\-control\fP \fIcolor_style/palette\fP[\fI/ncolors\fP] | \fIcptfile\fP
Color palette. \fIcolor_style\fP 1 gives a continuous palette, 2 a
discrete one. \fIpalette\fP is 1 Haxby colors, 2 high intensity
colors, 3 low intensity colors, 4 grayscale, 5 uniform gray, 6
uniform black or 7 uniform white; no color scale is drawn for 5-7.
\fIncolors\fP is the number of colors [11]. Default: 1/1, or 1/4
(grayscale) for color modes 4 and 5. If the argument names an existing
file, that file is used as the color palette table. With the default
order, the smallest values (the shallowest depths) get the first color
of the palette.
.TP
.B \-D\fP, \fB\-\-color\-flip
Reverse the color palette.
.TP
.B \-Y\fP, \fB\-\-no\-nice\-interval
Stretch the colors linearly over the data range instead of using
rounded color intervals.
.TP
.B \-S\fP, \fB\-\-stretch\-color
Set the color boundaries from the distribution of the plotted values
(\fBmbhistogram\fP), so that each color covers the same number of
values.
.TP
.B \-Z\fP, \fB\-\-zbounds\fP \fImin/max\fP
Range of the colored quantity: depth for color modes 1-3, amplitude for
mode 4, sidescan for mode 5. Default: the data range.
.TP
.B \-A\fP, \fB\-\-shade\fP \fImagnitude\fP[\fI/azimuth\fP | \fI/zero_level\fP]
Shading parameters in one argument, as in \fBmbm_plot \-A\fP:
magnitude and illumination azimuth for mode 2, or magnitude and the
amplitude of zero shading for mode 3 (\fBmbswath \-G\fP). The separate
options below take precedence.
.TP
.B \-\-magnitude\fP \fIval\fP
Shading magnitude. Defaults: 2.5 for mode 2; for mode 3, 2/(amax \-
amin) from the amplitude range, or 1 with \fB\-\-stretch\-shade\fP.
.TP
.B \-\-azimuth\fP \fIdeg\fP
Illumination azimuth for mode 2 [0].
.TP
.B \-\-zero\-level\fP \fIval\fP
Amplitude giving zero shading for mode 3. Default: amin + 0.2 (amax \-
amin), or 191 with \fB\-\-stretch\-shade\fP.
.TP
.B \-\-shade\-flip
Reverse the shading: for mode 2 the illumination azimuth is turned by
180 degrees; for a stretched mode 3 shade the gray scale is reversed.
.TP
.B \-\-stretch\-shade
Shade mode 3 maps with a gray scale fitted to a Gaussian distribution
of the amplitudes (\fBmbhistogram \-G\fP), written to
\fIroot\fP.shade.cpt and passed to \fBmbswath \-N\fP.
.TP
.B \-C\fP, \fB\-\-contour\fP [\fIcont_int/color_int/tick_int/label_int/tick_len/label_hgt\fP]
Plot bathymetry contours (\fBmbcontour \-A\fP) at \fIcont_int\fP,
with heavier contours every \fIcolor_int\fP, downhill ticks every
\fItick_int\fP and labels every \fIlabel_int\fP; \fItick_len\fP and
\fIlabel_hgt\fP are in inches. Missing fields get the defaults of
\fBmbm_plot\fP. With no argument, the contour interval is chosen from
the depth range, and the heavier contours, ticks and labels are every
fourth contour (or omitted when a swath image is also drawn).
.TP
.B \-\-contour\-algorithm\fP \fIn\fP
Contouring algorithm (\fBmbcontour \-Z\fP). Default: chosen by
\fBmbcontour\fP, except 1 for formats 41, 101 and 102.
.TP
.B \-\-contour\-nplot\fP \fIpings\fP
Number of pings contoured at a time (\fBmbcontour \-N\fP).
.TP
.B \-N\fP, \fB\-\-navigation\fP [\fItime_tick/time_annot/date_annot/tick_len\fP | \fBF\fP | \fBFP\fP]
Plot the ship track (\fBmbcontour \-D\fP), with ticks every
\fItime_tick\fP hours, time annotations every \fItime_annot\fP hours
and date annotations every \fIdate_annot\fP hours; \fItick_len\fP is in
inches. With no argument only the track is drawn. \fBF\fP annotates
the track with file names as well (\fBFP\fP perpendicular to the
track), with ticks every 0.25 hours.
.TP
.B \-\-nav\-names\fP [\fIheight\fP[\fI/P\fP]]
Annotate the track with file names of this height in inches [0.15];
\fI/P\fP places them perpendicular to the track.
.TP
.B \-\-ping\-ticks\fP [\fItick/annot/len\fP]
Mark ping numbers along the track (\fBmbcontour \-M\fP). Default
50/100/0.1.
.TP
.B \-\-footprint\fP \fIfactor/mode/depth\fP
Beam footprint parameters (\fBmbswath \-A\fP). Default 1.
.TP
.B \-\-swath\-scale\fP \fImode/scale\fP[\fI/min/max\fP]
Amplitude or sidescan scaling (\fBmbswath \-D\fP).
.TP
.B \-\-begin\-time\fP \fIyr/mo/da/hr/mn/sc\fP, \fB\-\-end\-time\fP \fIyr/mo/da/hr/mn/sc\fP
Plot only data inside this time window.
.TP
.B \-\-speedmin\fP \fIspeed\fP
Minimum ship speed in km/hr.
.TP
.B \-\-timegap\fP \fIminutes\fP
Time gap threshold.
.TP
.B \-\-lonflip\fP \fI\-1|0|1\fP
Longitude range: \-1 for \-360 to 0, 0 for \-180 to 180, 1 for 0 to
360. Default 0.
.TP
.B \-T\fP, \fB\-\-coast
Plot a coastline (\fBgmt coast\fP). If no coastline fill, pen, river
or boundary option is given, land is filled with gray 200 and the
coastline drawn with a 1p pen.
.TP
.B \-\-coast\-resolution\fP \fIres\fP
Coastline resolution: f, h, i, l or c. Default \fBf\fP.
.TP
.B \-\-coast\-dry\-fill\fP \fIcolor\fP, \fB\-\-coast\-wet\-fill\fP \fIcolor\fP, \fB\-\-coast\-lake\-fill\fP \fIcolor\fP
Fill land, water or lakes.
.TP
.B \-\-coast\-river\fP \fIspec\fP, \fB\-\-coast\-boundary\fP \fIspec\fP, \fB\-\-coast\-pen\fP \fIpen\fP
Draw rivers (\fBgmt coast \-I\fP), national boundaries (\fB\-N\fP,
repeatable) or the coastline (\fB\-W\fP).
.TP
.B \-\-xy\-overlay\fP \fIfile\fP[\fI:fill=color\fP][\fI:symbol=symbol\fP][\fI:pen=pen\fP]
Plot the lon/lat data in \fIfile\fP with \fBgmt plot\fP, as lines
(with a pen) or symbols; repeatable. Example:
"stations.xy:symbol=c0.1:fill=red".
.TP
.B \-\-text\fP \fIlon/lat/size/angle/font/justify/text\fP
Place a text label; repeatable. Example: "\-11.7/36.8/12/0/1/LB/Gorringe
Bank".
.TP
.B \-\-gmt\-default\fP \fIparam/value\fP
Override a GMT default parameter in the generated script; repeatable.

.SH EXAMPLES
A shaded relief map of the swath bathymetry in a datalist, with
contours and an annotated ship track, rendered at once to a PNG:

.br
 mbpy_plot \-I datalist.mb\-1 \-G2 \-C \-N 0.25/1/4 \\
.br
     \-\-format png \-X \-V

A sidescan map of one file with an equalized grayscale stretch:

.br
 mbpy_plot \-I 0003_20111219_180559_METEOR_EM122p.mb59 \-G5 \-S

A track map with file names, a coastline and a distance scale at the
map center:

.br
 mbpy_plot \-I datalist.mb\-1 \-N F \-T \\
.br
     \-\-length\-scale "gcenter+c36.8+w5k"

